Test clips for ../test-video-padding.c: 3 pictures each of FFmpeg's testsrc2, made with
FFmpeg 8 (libvpx 1.15, SVT-AV1 4.2):

  src="testsrc2=size=WxH:rate=30,format=yuv420p"            (vp9p2: yuv420p10le)
  ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "$src" -frames:v 3 -c:v libvpx-vp9 -profile:v 0 -auto-alt-ref 0 \
    -lag-in-frames 0 -g 3 -crf 50 -b:v 0 -deadline realtime -cpu-used 8 -f ivf vp9p0-WxH.ivf
  ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "$src" -frames:v 3 -c:v libsvtav1 -preset 12 -g 3 -crf 50 \
    -svtav1-params "pred-struct=1:enable-overlays=0" -f ivf av1-320x180.ivf
  321x181: testsrc2 at 322x182, then format=yuv420p,crop=321:181:0:0:exact=1

The test's hashes are FNV-1a over the last picture as FFmpeg's software decoder makes it
(libvpx-vp9 / dav1d), Y rows then UV interleaved, 10-bit as P010 (value << 6, little
endian). A new clip needs its hash from the same sum.
